            "description": "Watch Belgrano Cordoba vs Sarmiento Junin highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 3, 2026. On May 3, 2026 , the Liga Profesional Argentina spotlight fell on the clash between Belgrano Cordoba and Sarmiento Junin . Both teams entered the match with everything to play for, creating an electric atmosphere as the players took to the pitch for this crucial mid-season fixture. A Frantic Opening and First-Half Breakthrough The match began with high intensity as both sides looked to establish control in the midfield. Sarmiento faced early pressure, leading to a yellow card for Santiago Salle in the 24th minute as he struggled to contain the Belgrano attack. The home side's persistence finally paid off in the 36th minute when Francisco Gonzalez Metilli found the back of the net after a perfectly weighted pass from Lucas Passerini . The goal prompted an immediate tactical shift from the visitors, who replaced Agustin Seyral with Manuel Garcia in an attempt to stabilize their formation. The closing stages of the first half proved difficult for the visitors. Just minutes after Agustin Falcon received a yellow card for a mistimed challenge, the pressure from the Cordoba outfit forced a significant error in the Sarmiento box. In the 43rd minute, defender Lucas Suarez inadvertently turned the ball into his own net, doubling Belgrano's advantage. This own goal left the visitors reeling as they headed into the tunnel for the halftime break, facing a steep mountain to climb in the second period. Belgrano Maintains the Pressure Seeking a spark to ignite a comeback, Sarmiento introduced Julian Contrera for Pablo Magnin at the start of the second half. However, the momentum remained firmly with the hosts. In the 55th minute, Belgrano further extended their lead through a well-worked move. Adrian Sanchez provided a clinical assist for Ramiro Hernandes , who made no mistake with his finish to effectively put the result beyond doubt. The goal showcased the fluid attacking football that had characterized the home side's performance throughout the afternoon. With the match comfortably in hand, the Belgrano coaching staff opted for a series of tactical substitutions in the 65th minute to maintain their energy levels. Franco Vazquez , Lucas Zelarayan , and Ramiro Tulian were introduced to replace Santiago Longo , Emiliano Ariel Rigoni , and goalscorer Ramiro Hernandes . Sarmiento also looked to their bench, bringing on Diego Churin and Juan Cabrera , but they struggled to find any rhythm against a disciplined and organized opposition defense. Late Flourish and Final Whistle As the clock ticked toward the 90-minute mark, the fresh legs of the substitutes played a decisive role in the final scoring action of the game. In the 86th minute, Ramiro Tulian capped off an impressive team performance by scoring the fourth goal for Belgrano . His strike was the final blow to a weary Sarmiento defense that had been under siege for most of the contest. The visitors attempted to find a late consolation, but the defensive line led by the hosts remained resolute until the final whistle. The referee brought the proceedings to an end in the first minute of stoppage time, confirming a comprehensive victory for the Cordoba-based club. For Belgrano , the match was a demonstration of clinical finishing and defensive solidity, while Sarmiento will be left to reflect on defensive lapses and an inability to convert their limited chances into meaningful pressure."
        },
